  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Cut inside – curved run and drive to the middle",
  "description": "Four lines: A and D in the corners by the goal, B and C further out along the sides. A runs in a curve along the board and gets a pass from B level with the cone. A receives, curves in with the ball towards the middle and shoots. Then D runs from the other side and gets the pass from C.\n\nRotation: B goes to line A, A to D, D to C and C to B. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Receive on the move – do not stop at the cone."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Cut in towards the middle with the ball close to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shoot as soon as you have a good angle."
    }
  ],
